    "Scouting Notes": "Starter\n Fastball sitting 93-95 this year and generating a lot of whiffs up in the zone\n Curve and slider are both looking strong in terms of movement, but they are both a bit inconsistent in terms of command and can lose the shape at times too\n Changeup has come around a little, but a distant fourth pitch\n Command shows flashes, but will likely always be a below average walk type of guy, average at best",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/2/0223",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "DRAFT REPORT\nKnoth might have the highest ceiling of the Brewer's day 1 selections. His profile was extremely enticing, even when he only threw his fastball in the 90-93 range (T95) last summer. This spring however, he was up to 98 and sitting more in the 94-95 range. The fastball has good life at the top of the zone and pairs exceptionally well with what might be the best secondary offering in the entire system the moment Knoth signs. That offering is his hammer curveball. It’s a 3000 RPM pitch with late bite and a ton of movement. He has a smooth delivery that appears to be easily repeatable. Still only 17, Knoth’s upside on the mound might be second only to Jacob Misiorowski in the Brewers system",
